{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>For the islands shall hope in Me.</b> That I shall give them good reward:" "<b>And ships of Tarshish as at first.</b> And he mentioned Tarshish because it is close to the land:" "<b>Their silver and their gold.</b> Now the meaning is: for the islands shall hope in Me, for Israel will not give them wages, and behold it is explained: for the name of YHWH your Elohim:" "Now <b>your splendor.</b> comes with kamatz gadol instead of kamatz katan because it is the end of a verse:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 60, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:27.821597506Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}